notifyT -- which writes tell a field's listeners (Tony, 2026-11-12, SEQ 629: arithmetic writes notify, guarded, with a
re-entry guard). One listener per notifier; each listener's action bumps a counter, zeroed before each write.

fires     every write that changes a value: =, +=, *=, /=, ++ and -- (prefix), on a count and on a number; text = and +=;
          := on a holder. Before this stroke count += *= ++ -- and number += *= fired nothing: they write the raw count
          or number, and only the setters called updateListeners.
quiet     +% (an attach) and :. (a flag) change no value and fire nothing.
minus     PINNED AT TODAY'S VALUE, NOT CURED: -= on a listened-to field does not subtract and so does not fire. opMinusEQ
          asks first whether the target holds a list, and the listener list is an attribute, so it takes the
          remove-a-member arm. The same happens to any valued field with an attribute. Intended: 1 fire, value 8 lower.
reentry   a listener whose action writes its own notifier (with = and with +=) fires once per outside write and the run
          ends: updateListeners takes hasListeners down for its walk. H7 (run under an alarm, 2026-11-12): in the commit.
jitted    MEASURED, NOT RULED: a jitted action that writes a listened-to field twice (= then +=) fires the listener ONCE a
          run, on its first run and on a refire; the interpreted twin fires twice. The value is right on both. Which of the
          two writes tells the listener was not chased.
